description:
Every sibling extension type crate in the workspace exposes a pub const for its capability URI:

  - jmap-metadata-types: pub const JMAP_METADATA_URI: &str = \"urn:ietf:params:jmap:metadata\";
  - jmap-filenode-types: pub const JMAP_FILENODE_URI: &str = \"urn:ietf:params:jmap:filenode\";
  - jmap-contacts-types: pub const JMAP_CONTACTS_URI: &str = \"urn:ietf:params:jmap:contacts\";
  - jmap-calendars-types: pub const JMAP_CALENDARS_URI: &str = \"urn:ietf:params:jmap:calendars\";
  - jmap-tasks-types: pub const JMAP_TASKS_URI plus 5 sub-capability URIs
  - jmap-sharing-types: pub const JMAP_PRINCIPALS_URI, JMAP_PRINCIPALS_OWNER_URI
  - jmap-mail-types: pub const JMAP_MDN_URI, JMAP_SIEVE_SCRIPTS_URI

…with re-exports from lib.rs and a one-line literal-equality test in tests/. crate-jmap-cid-types has none of these — neither in src/ nor in lib.rs re-exports. The URI is mentioned only in rustdoc prose.

API-contract impact: every downstream consumer (jmap-base-client::Session::supports_cid(), jmap-chat-types' attachment-sha256 binding, a future jmap-filenode-types FileNode binding, any third-party CID consumer) will hardcode the literal string \"urn:ietf:params:jmap:cid\". If the literal differs by one character — and capability URIs are notoriously easy to typo (cid vs cid, capital letters, missing colon) — capability detection silently fails. Without a constant, the maintainer cannot enforce a single source of truth.

This is the workspace canonical-templates rule (workspace AGENTS.md \"Canonical Templates\") applied to a missing constant. PLAN.md §\"Public API (current state)\" already anticipates the CidCapability struct in capability.rs; the URI constant should land in the same module the same way every sibling does.

Suggested layout (matching jmap-metadata-types/src/capability.rs):

    pub const JMAP_CID_URI: &str = \"urn:ietf:params:jmap:cid\";

…re-exported from lib.rs alongside the eventual CidCapability struct (finding .6). Worth landing before v0.1.0 publishes, because once consumers code against the literal, swapping to the constant is a coordinated edit across every consumer crate.
